Feature: Update volume paths in pyspark_script.py using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx

  The system must update only the volume paths in pyspark_script.py according to the mapping provided in volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx. All other code logic, structure, and variable names must remain unchanged.

  Background:
    Given pyspark_script.py contains hardcoded volume paths for biomarker_readings.csv, patient_demographics.csv, and site_details.csv
    And volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx provides a one-to-one mapping of old_volume_path to new_volume_path for each file

  Scenario Outline: Replace old volume paths with new volume paths in pyspark_script.py
    Given the script contains the old volume path "<old_volume_path>"
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then the script must contain the new volume path "<new_volume_path>"
    And no other part of the script is changed

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                 | new_volume_path                                                                                                 |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv         | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv         |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv        | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv         |

  Scenario: Happy path - All volume paths are present in mapping sheet and replaced successfully
    Given pyspark_script.py contains all three old volume paths as per the mapping sheet
    When the update logic is executed
    Then all three old volume paths are replaced with their corresponding new volume paths
    And the rest of the script remains unchanged

  Scenario: Error - Old volume path not found in mapping sheet
    Given pyspark_script.py contains a volume path "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/unknown_file.csv"
    And volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx does not contain a mapping for "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/unknown_file.csv"
    When the update logic is executed
    Then the script must not change the path "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/unknown_file.csv"
    And an error message "No mapping found for volume path: /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/unknown_file.csv" is logged

  Scenario: Error - Mapping sheet is missing or unreadable
    Given volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx is missing or cannot be read
    When the update logic is executed
    Then no changes are made to pyspark_script.py
    And an error message "Volume mapping sheet not found or unreadable" is logged

  Scenario: Validation - Only volume paths are changed, no other code is modified
    Given pyspark_script.py contains code logic, variable names, and comments
    When the update logic is executed
    Then only the volume paths specified in the mapping sheet are changed
    And all other code logic, variable names, and comments remain unchanged

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven test for multiple volume path replacements
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the old volume path "<old_volume_path>"
    And volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx maps "<old_volume_path>" to "<new_volume_path>"
    When the update logic is executed
    Then the script contains "<new_volume_path>" instead of "<old_volume_path>"

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                 | new_volume_path                                                                                                 |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv         | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv         |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv        | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv         |

  Scenario: Validation - Data format and path correctness
    Given the new volume path is in the format "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/<file_name>.csv"
    When the update logic is executed
    Then the script must use the new path in the correct format for each file

  Scenario: Error - Duplicate old volume paths in script
    Given pyspark_script.py contains duplicate occurrences of "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv"
    And volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx maps it to "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv"
    When the update logic is executed
    Then all occurrences of the old volume path are replaced with the new volume path

  Scenario: Error - Invalid new volume path in mapping sheet
    Given volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains a new_volume_path "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/"
    When the update logic is executed
    Then an error message "Invalid new volume path for mapping: /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/" is logged
    And the old volume path is not replaced

  Scenario: Validation - No extra whitespace or formatting changes
    Given pyspark_script.py contains old volume paths with no extra whitespace
    When the update logic is executed
    Then the new volume paths are inserted without extra whitespace or formatting changes

  Scenario: Validation - Logging of changes
    Given the update logic is executed
    When a volume path is replaced
    Then a log entry "Replaced <old_volume_path> with <new_volume_path>" is created for each change

